  "motto": [
   "Many feet. One message.",
   "Every nation in view."
  ],
  "lead": {
   "k": "p",
   "runs": [
    "In a courtroom, a witness is someone who tells what they have seen and know. The New Testament uses the same word for people who tell others about Jesus. They tell who He is, what He did, and why it matters. This study is about that telling, done by one friend to another and carried by whole churches to the far side of the world. It teaches one reading habit. ",
    {
     "b": "In any passage about witness, ask whose part is whose."
    },
    " What does God do? What is given to the person who speaks? What belongs to the person who hears? Most mistakes about witness come from mixing these up. One mistake is pressing people as if their answer were ours to produce. The other is staying silent as if speaking were not ours to do."
   ]
  },
  "verse": {
   "k": "quote",
   "r": "1CO.3.6",
   "label": "1 Corinthians 3:6",
   "t": "I planted the seed and Apollos watered it, but God made it grow."
  },
  "selection": {
   "k": "p",
   "runs": [
    "This is a selection, not a census. It walks seven passages: the risen Jesus’ charge on a mountain in Galilee, two paragraphs from Romans, two from Paul’s letters to Corinth, one from Philippians and one from Colossians. Each was chosen because it answers a different question about telling others: why, what, to whom, by what means, at what cost and in what manner. A few other verses are quoted for one point each, and the studies that read them in full are linked. Paul’s prayers for open doors belong to ",
    {
     "s": "../prayer-in-the-letters-directions/",
     "t": "Prayer across Scripture: learning to pray"
    },
    ". Peter’s words on answering with gentleness belong to ",
    {
     "s": "../faith-under-pressure-directions/",
     "t": "Faith under pressure"
    },
    ". The good news itself, told in full, is the subject of ",
    {
     "s": "../the-good-news-directions/",
     "t": "The good news: how a person is made right with God"
    },
    ". This page is not a method that guarantees results, because no passage here offers one."
   ]
  },
